    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# This documents the constraint for your README/portfolio writeup.\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\"\"\n",
        "REALISTIC CONSTRAINT IMPLEMENTED:\n",
        "Dynamic access-level escalation.\n",
        "\n",
        "Problem: In a real bank, a document's sensitivity can change after it has\n",
        "already been indexed - e.g., a customer's risk rating changes following\n",
        "an AML review, and previously Internal-level content about that customer\n",
        "should immediately become AML-Confidential.\n",
        "\n",
        "Solution: escalate_access_level() updates a document's access_level\n",
        "in-place inside ChromaDB (not just in a separate rules table), so every\n",
        "subsequent query - regardless of when the document was originally\n",
        "ingested - respects the CURRENT classification, not the one assigned at\n",
        "ingestion time.\n",
        "\n",
        "Proof: CALL-012 (Imran Shaikh's routine call) was Internal and visible to\n",
        "branch officers. After simulating the AML escalation documented in\n",
        "CHAT-012, the same query with the same role returns zero results from\n",
        "CALL-012, while compliance_officer retrieval is unaffected.\n",
        "\"\"\")"
